// `v.push(1)` on a `let v: Vec<i64>` (no `mut`): E0596 — the bare-place `&mut self` receiver asks the binding-mut question (was ADMITTED).
// PROBES.md 2026-09-08a: a place in a mutable-use position takes the DerefMut/IndexMut step at every level, a Deref-only/Index-only step is refused, and the bare `deref_mut()` receiver is asked the binding-mut question.
package bc_mutplace_vec_push_immut_binding_fail;
fn main() -> i32 {
    let v: Vec<i64> = Vec::new();
    v.push(1i64);
    return 0i32;
}
